Restore the panel when main() returns before reaching Display::close().

Every early `return 1` after open_displays() (an unreadable ROM, a refused
--load-state, a JIT attach failure, a bad record/replay file) destroys the
Display without calling close(). Neither scanout tier has a destructor, so:

  DispOut   the presenter thread is still joinable when std::thread is
            destroyed, which calls std::terminate; and the UI layer open()
            disabled is never re-enabled, so the launcher that runs next
            draws into a layer nobody sees and the panel stays dark until a
            reboot.
  FbdevOut  the same std::terminate, and fb0 is left on whatever pan offset
            the presenter last set.

Both close() methods are already idempotent, so a destructor that calls it
changes nothing on the normal exit path, where Display::close() has already
closed and released the tier. It also cleans up after a tier whose open()
fails inside Display::open.

Display itself gets no destructor on purpose: the early returns call
SDL_Quit() first, and destroying its textures and window after that would
touch freed SDL objects.

Not a toolchain workaround; drop once upstream fixes it.

Upstream: https://github.com/beebono/DSperate/issues/21

diff --git a/src/frontend/sdl/display_disp.h b/src/frontend/sdl/display_disp.h
index 31156ff..13adcec 100644
--- a/src/frontend/sdl/display_disp.h
+++ b/src/frontend/sdl/display_disp.h
@@ -82,6 +82,10 @@ public:
   // nothing changed on the device.
   bool open(int rot, bool vsync);
   void close();
+  // An early return from main() never reaches Display::close(). Without this
+  // the joinable presenter thread calls std::terminate, and the UI layer
+  // open() disabled stays off, leaving the next program on a dark panel.
+  ~DispOut() { close(); }
   bool vsync() const { return vsync_; }
 
   // The canvas: the layout's natural size at scale 1 (Display::natural_size),
diff --git a/src/frontend/sdl/display_fbdev.h b/src/frontend/sdl/display_fbdev.h
index af0a9dd..59c9774 100644
--- a/src/frontend/sdl/display_fbdev.h
+++ b/src/frontend/sdl/display_fbdev.h
@@ -63,6 +63,10 @@ public:
   // on the headless driver (a fullscreen toggle) is simply re-asserted.
   bool reopen(SDL_Window* win, int w, int h) override;
   void close() override;
+  // An early return from main() never reaches Display::close(). Without this
+  // the joinable presenter thread calls std::terminate, and fb0 is left on a
+  // pan offset the next program does not expect.
+  ~FbdevOut() override { close(); }
 
   int width() const override { return w_; }
   int height() const override { return h_; }
